hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"193","On gifts: al-Abbas ibn al-Walid ibn Mazyad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from al-Awza'i, who said: al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Urwah, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: There is revoked from the charity of one who acts unjustly in his life what is revoked from the bequest of one who acts unjustly at his death. al-Abbas said: He narrated it to us once from Urwah, and once from Urwah, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abu Dawud said: This hadith is not sound; its raising to the Prophet is not sound."
"194","Sulayman ibn Dawud [al-Mahri] narrated to us, Ibn Wahb informed us; Yunus ibn Yazid and Ibn Sam'an informed me, from Ibn Shihab, who said: There is revoked from the injustice of a living giver in his life what is revoked from the injustice of a dead person in his bequest at his death."
"195","Muhammad ibn Yahya [ibn Faris] narrated to me, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to me, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, who said: There is revoked from the injustice of a living giver what is revoked from the injustice of a dead person in his bequest. Abu Dawud said: al-Hiql narrated it from al-Awza'i, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, as a stopped report."
